          "text": "Define $C_n$ to be the minimum cost to acquire a total rod length of exactly $n$ meters. You can purchase rods of standard integer lengths, and for $i&gt;0$, let $\\operatorname{cost}[i]$ denote the purchase price of a rod whose length is $i$ meters. You can combine multiple purchased rods to achieve the target length $n$.<br>\n<br>\nConsider the array of costs for standard lengths:<br>\n<br>\n$$<br>\n\\operatorname{cost}[1]=2, \\operatorname{cost}[2]=5, \\operatorname{cost}[3]=7, \\operatorname{cost}[4]=8<br>\n$$<br>\n<br>\nWhat is the minimum cost $C_8$ to acquire a total length of 8 meters, with the additional constraint that you are allowed to purchase at most three rods in total?",
